IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `je21-nouns`

-- je21-part3a-consolidation: Articles 12 to 14 of the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021 (L.8/2021):
-- 12 Types of legislation under this Part, 13 Consolidated legislation, 14 Editorial changes.
--
-- The duties of the Principal Legislative Drafter in these Articles matter to the reader of an enactment through what they produce:
-- whether a consolidated version will exist (13(1)), whether it says what it is (13(2)), and whether an editorial change to it can alter what the legislation means (14(2)).
-- Article 14(4) is a saving for other authority, and the Law gives it no content a reader could ask about (NOTES.md section 4).
--
-- 13(1) turns on "after the commencement of this Part", which for an event on 28 September 2021 itself depends on the time at which Part 3 came into force: fork L3.

§ `Article 12 -- Types of legislation under this Part`

-- Answers: is this text as-enacted legislation?
-- It is if it contains the text of the legislation as originally made, or is that legislation in the form it appears when prepared for publication under Part 3.
-- src:121 | (2) As-enacted legislation is legislation containing the text of the legislation as originally made and includes that legislation in the form it appears when prepared for publication under this Part.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 12(2) (src:121)
GIVEN `it contains the text of the legislation as originally made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is that legislation in the form it appears when prepared for publication under Part 3` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 12(2): the text is as-enacted legislation` `it contains the text of the legislation as originally made` `it is that legislation in the form it appears when prepared for publication under Part 3` MEANS
        `it contains the text of the legislation as originally made`
    OR  `it is that legislation in the form it appears when prepared for publication under Part 3`

-- Answers: is this text consolidated legislation?
-- It is if it includes the modifications necessary to show the legislation as it was in force on the date to which it is stated to be consolidated (12(3)), and revised legislation is also consolidated legislation (12(4)).
-- src:122 | (3) Consolidated legislation is legislation that includes within it any other modifications necessary to show the legislation as it was in force on the date to which it is stated to be consolidated.
-- src:123 | (4) Revised legislation is also consolidated legislation.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 12(3) and (4) (src:122-123)
GIVEN `it includes the modifications necessary to show the legislation as it was in force on the date to which it is stated to be consolidated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is revised legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 12(3) and (4): the text is consolidated legislation` `it includes the modifications necessary to show the legislation as it was in force on the date to which it is stated to be consolidated` `it is revised legislation` MEANS
        `it includes the modifications necessary to show the legislation as it was in force on the date to which it is stated to be consolidated`
    OR  `it is revised legislation`

-- Answers: does Part 3 apply in respect of this kind of text?
-- It applies to as-enacted legislation and to consolidated legislation, and revised legislation is consolidated legislation.
-- src:118 | (1) This Part applies in respect of –
-- src:119 | (a) as-enacted legislation; and
-- src:120 | (b) consolidated legislation.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 12(1) (src:118-120)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of text under Part 3`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 12(1): Part 3 applies in respect of the text` kind MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `as-enacted legislation` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `consolidated legislation` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `revised legislation` THEN TRUE

§ `Article 13 -- Consolidated legislation`

§§ `13(1) The duty to prepare a consolidated version`

-- Answers: must the Principal Legislative Drafter prepare a consolidated version of this legislation?
-- Yes, as soon as practicable, when Jersey legislation is commenced, amended or revised after the commencement of Part 3,
-- unless it is legislation having the effect only to amend or commence other legislation, or an Act of the States referred to in Article 2(2).
-- "after the commencement of this Part": an event on 28 September 2021 itself is after the beginning of that day on the default reading (L3), and refused on the other.
-- FALSE means Article 13(1) does not require a consolidated version.
-- src:125 | (1) When any Jersey legislation (other than legislation having the effect only to amend or commence other legislation or consisting of an Act of the States referred to in Article 2(2)) is commenced, amended or revised after the commencement of this Part, the Principal Legislative Drafter must, as soon as practicable, prepare a consolidated version of the legislation.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 13(1) (src:125)
GIVEN `it is Jersey legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has the effect only to amend or commence other legislation, or consists of an Act of the States referred to in Article 2(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      event IS AN `Event that calls for a consolidated version`
      `the day on which the event happened` IS A DATE
      reading IS A `Reading L3 of the time at which the Law came into force`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 13(1): the Principal Legislative Drafter must prepare a consolidated version` `it is Jersey legislation` `it has the effect only to amend or commence other legislation, or consists of an Act of the States referred to in Article 2(2)` event `the day on which the event happened` reading MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `it is Jersey legislation` THEN FALSE
        IF `it has the effect only to amend or commence other legislation, or consists of an Act of the States referred to in Article 2(2)` THEN FALSE
        IF event EQUALS `none of these has happened` THEN FALSE
        IF `the day on which the event happened` LESS THAN YMD 2021 9 28 THEN FALSE
        IF `the day on which the event happened` GREATER THAN YMD 2021 9 28 THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER reading
            WHEN `the beginning of 28 September 2021, by Article 3(2)` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `the sources do not state it, so a question that turns on a time of day on 28 September 2021 is refused`
                THEN REFUSE "the sources do not say at what time of day on 28 September 2021 Part 3 of the Law came into force, so whether an event that day was after it cannot be answered"

§§ `13(2) What a consolidated version must say`

-- Answers: does the consolidated legislation carry the statement Article 13(2) requires?
-- It must include a statement that it is consolidated legislation compiled under the authority of the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021.
-- Anything that is not consolidated legislation is outside the paragraph, and the model refuses.
-- src:126 | (2) Consolidated legislation must include a statement that it is consolidated legislation compiled under the authority of this Law.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 13(2) (src:126)
GIVEN `the text is consolidated legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it includes a statement that it is consolidated legislation compiled under the authority of the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 13(2): the consolidated legislation includes the statement the Law requires` `the text is consolidated legislation` `it includes a statement that it is consolidated legislation compiled under the authority of the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021` MEANS
    IF `the text is consolidated legislation`
    THEN `it includes a statement that it is consolidated legislation compiled under the authority of the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021`
    ELSE REFUSE "Article 13(2) speaks of consolidated legislation, and the text is not consolidated legislation"

§ `Article 14 -- Editorial changes`

§§ `14(1) The editorial changes the Principal Legislative Drafter may make`

-- Answers: may the Principal Legislative Drafter make this change to this text?
-- Any of the changes in (a) to (e), to consolidated legislation, whether when preparing it or later.
-- (c), the removal of a provision the Principal Legislative Drafter "considers to be spent or for any other reason to be no longer operative", rests on that consideration, and the change is described that way.
-- src:128 | (1) The Principal Legislative Drafter may make the following changes to consolidated legislation (whether when preparing it or later) –
-- src:129 | (a) the removal of a provision relating to its commencement;
-- src:130 | (b) the removal of a provision that amends or repeals other legislation (or any provision of that other legislation);
-- src:131 | (c) the removal of any other provision that the Principal Legislative Drafter considers to be spent or for any other reason to be no longer operative;
-- src:132 | (d) the correction of –
-- src:133 | (i) typographical and clerical errors,
-- src:134 | (ii) errors in grammar, spelling and punctuation,
-- src:135 | (iii) errors in numbering, cross-referencing, and alphabetical ordering,
-- src:136 | (iv) errors in, or arising out of, an amendment by other legislation to the legislation being consolidated, and
-- src:137 | (v) any other errors of a similar nature;
-- src:138 | (e) changes in punctuation and the relocation of conjunctives or disjunctives to enable the addition or removal of any provision that is or was part of a list of provisions.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 14(1) (src:128-138)
GIVEN change IS AN `Editorial change under Article 14(1)`
      `the text is consolidated legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 14(1): the Principal Legislative Drafter may make the change` change `the text is consolidated legislation` MEANS
    CONSIDER change
    WHEN `the removal of a provision relating to its commencement` THEN `the text is consolidated legislation`
    WHEN `the removal of a provision that amends or repeals other legislation` THEN `the text is consolidated legislation`
    WHEN `the removal of another provision that the Principal Legislative Drafter considers spent or no longer operative` THEN `the text is consolidated legislation`
    WHEN `the correction of typographical and clerical errors` THEN `the text is consolidated legislation`
    WHEN `the correction of errors in grammar, spelling and punctuation` THEN `the text is consolidated legislation`
    WHEN `the correction of errors in numbering, cross-referencing and alphabetical ordering` THEN `the text is consolidated legislation`
    WHEN `the correction of errors in, or arising out of, an amendment by other legislation` THEN `the text is consolidated legislation`
    WHEN `the correction of any other errors of a similar nature` THEN `the text is consolidated legislation`
    WHEN `changes in punctuation, and the relocation of conjunctives or disjunctives, to add or remove a provision in a list` THEN `the text is consolidated legislation`

§§ `14(2) No change has effect to the extent of changing a meaning`

-- Answers: does the change have effect in full?
-- "none of these changes has effect to the extent of changing the meaning of any provision": a change that would alter the meaning of a provision has no effect to that extent.
-- TRUE means it has effect in full.
-- FALSE means it has no effect to the extent that it changes a meaning, and the Law does not say how much of the change that is.
-- src:139 | (2) However, none of these changes has effect to the extent of changing the meaning of any provision.[3]
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 14(2) (src:139)
GIVEN `the change would alter the meaning of a provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 14(2): the editorial change has effect in full` `the change would alter the meaning of a provision` MEANS
    NOT `the change would alter the meaning of a provision`

§§ `14(3) Formatting and presentational changes`

-- Answers: may the Principal Legislative Drafter make this formatting or presentational change?
-- The authority is to make them "so that consolidated legislation is consistent with current drafting practice".
-- Paragraph (2) speaks of "these changes", the changes of paragraph (1), and paragraph (3) has no limit of its own on meaning.
-- src:140 | (3) The Principal Legislative Drafter may make formatting and presentational changes to the legislation so that consolidated legislation is consistent with current drafting practice.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 14(3) (src:140)
GIVEN `the text is consolidated legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the change is made so that the legislation is consistent with current drafting practice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 14(3): the Principal Legislative Drafter may make the formatting or presentational change` `the text is consolidated legislation` `the change is made so that the legislation is consistent with current drafting practice` MEANS
        `the text is consolidated legislation`
    AND `the change is made so that the legislation is consistent with current drafting practice`

§§ `14(5) Changes that must be set out`

-- Answers: must this change be set out in an endnote or other suitable place?
-- A change authorised by Article 14 must, other than a formatting or presentational change or a minor editorial change.
-- src:142 | (5) Changes authorised by this Article that are made to consolidated legislation, other than formatting and presentational changes or minor editorial changes, must be set out in an endnote or other suitable place.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 14(5) (src:142)
GIVEN `it is a formatting or presentational change` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a minor editorial change` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 14(5): the change must be set out in an endnote or other suitable place` `it is a formatting or presentational change` `it is a minor editorial change` MEANS
        NOT `it is a formatting or presentational change`
    AND NOT `it is a minor editorial change`

§§ `14(6) Correcting errors in a published version`

-- Answers: may the Principal Legislative Drafter correct this error in this published version?
-- An error in a published version of as-enacted legislation that occurred after it was made, or in revised legislation that occurred after its revision.
-- FALSE means Article 14(6) does not give the power.
-- src:143 | (6) The Principal Legislative Drafter may correct any errors in a published version of as-enacted legislation that occurred after it is made or in revised legislation that occurred after its revision.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 14(6) (src:143)
GIVEN version IS A `Published version for Article 14(6)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 14(6): the Principal Legislative Drafter may correct the error` version MEANS
    CONSIDER version
    WHEN `a published version of as-enacted legislation, with an error that occurred after it was made` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a published version of revised legislation, with an error that occurred after its revision` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `any other published version or error` THEN FALSE
